{"address": "714 State St", "attributes": {"Ambience": null, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": false, "street": false, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "RestaurantsReservations": true, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": null}, "business_stars": 3.0, "categories": "Restaurants, Sushi Bars", "city": "Santa Barbara", "hours": null, "name": "Piranha Restaurant & Sushi Bar", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2008-08-08 19:51:46", "review_stars": 4.0, "review_text": "The sushi was mediocre but I still like the environment and the service!"}, {"review_date": "2008-07-26 05:03:21", "review_stars": 2.0, "review_text": ""after a lovely day at the beach, my husband and i decided to finish off the day with some sushi. we'd eaten at piranha before and enjoyed it, but after tonight's experience, i can safely say we will never return. it wasn't heinous--but for 80$, the quality of the food and service was pretty abysmal. not only was the sushi NOT super fresh and tasty, especially as compared to katsuya in encino, but the waitstaff was inattentive (we had to call out for the hostess finally to get our waitress's attention), the waitress made a mistake on our order and did not recitfy it (she brought out sea urchin instead of eel--when we brought it to her attention, she did not remove the unwanted, uneaten item from our bill), AND there was a long hair in one of our rolls! At most sushi establishments, they bring out the items as they are prepared, but here, we had to wait a fairly long time before  being served, and then it was everything, all at once.  Plus, i really like it when the meal commences with a nice, warm hand towel and some complimentary edaname--typical of most sushi places, but NOT here. Overall, a very unpleasant, unappetizing, unsatisfying gastronomical experience!""}, {"review_date": "2008-06-02 15:01:40", "review_stars": 4.0, "review_text": "This is a nice place to sit outside on State St.  I was a tad bit early for sushi (they don't start making sushi until 5:30), so I decided on their Warm Spinach Salad instead.  It was deeeelish.  I had a blackberry martini to sip on, which was also really good.  The server was really nice and attentive the entire time.  

I've also been here previously and have sat in their outside area upstairs, which is also nice.  

I'm curious to try their sushi soon, which might alter my rating."}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "608 Anacapa St", "attributes": {"Ambience": {"casual": true, "classy": false, "divey": false, "hipster": false, "intimate": false, "romantic": true, "touristy": false, "trendy": false, "upscale": false}, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": false, "street": false, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "RestaurantsReservations": true, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": "free"}, "business_stars": 4.5, "categories": "Sandwiches, Delis, Pizza, Italian, Restaurants", "city": "Santa Barbara", "hours": {"Friday": "11:0-21:30", "Saturday": "11:0-21:30", "Sunday": "16:0-21:0", "Thursday": "11:0-21:0", "Tuesday": "11:0-21:0", "Wednesday": "11:0-21:0"}, "name": "Basil's Italian", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2018-10-22 02:03:20", "review_stars": 4.0, "review_text": "Went tonight to find the place closed  - looks like for good. Everything was gone but tables and chairs. Sad - it became our go to Italian place."}, {"review_date": "2018-10-06 03:20:21", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "This place is amazing. If you want great authentic Italian and warm friendly service... this is where you need to be. It blows my mind more people don't know how good this place is. Top 3 Italian in town for sure: the complimentary bread is amazing. The wine... delicious and my tummy is never unhappy leaving here. JUST COME!! You will not regret it :) love you basil's!!"}, {"review_date": "2018-09-28 21:22:14", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Off the beaten path but well worth a visit!

Had lunch here today. The sweet server brought out some soft foccacia bread. Combo pizza was hot and loaded with fresh toppings. Egg plant parmesan was Panko breaded and topped with a rich tomato sauce with delicious pasta on the side. 

Shout out to Rosemary...thank you!"}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "141-153 Harbor Way", "attributes": {"Ambience": {"casual": false, "classy": false, "divey": false, "hipster": false, "intimate": false, "romantic": false, "touristy": false, "trendy": false, "upscale": false}, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": true, "street": false, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": null, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "RestaurantsTakeOut": null, "WiFi": "no"}, "business_stars": 4.5, "categories": "Food, Local Flavor, Seafood, Arts & Entertainment, Shopping, Festivals, Restaurants, Arts & Crafts", "city": "Santa Barbara", "hours": {"Saturday": "10:0-17:0"}, "name": "Santa Barbara Harbor & Seafood Festival", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2021-09-08 22:31:44", "review_stars": 4.0, "review_text": "Beach shack for takeout on one side and casual dine-in restaurant on the other side.  We had the ceviche, albacore tuna melt and ahi tacos. All were very good and we'd get them again! Ordered the bartender special cocktail - good but a little pricey and served in a martini glass so not a lot of cocktail.  All in all, a fun place with decent food."}, {"review_date": "2019-10-15 00:23:03", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "We flew to LAX 1 day before, and drove 2 hours from LA to Santa Barbara which is our trip main itinerary. There are several tents selling merchandise along from parking lot to pier. On the pier, you can get fresh sea urchin, crabs, and spiky lobsters. Lobsters each weighs over 1 lb to almost 2 lbs. You just hand picked and paid by the weight which they accept credit card. Then you proceed to cook station for fee of $5 and waited for about an hour. We also got a plate of paella, a cup of clam chowder for our lunch. Initially wanted to try fresh oysters a dozen for $25 but the line was too long. There's ceviche, taco, street corn, etc. Once we got our food, we settled down near the beach picnic table under palm trees. 

All and all, the experience was great. Enjoyed driving along beach despite the LA traffic."}, {"review_date": "2019-10-14 01:18:58", "review_stars": 2.0, "review_text": "Over crowded festival with overpriced food. I was mainly interested in tasting some fresh uni.  There were a couple of venders selling live uni but most of them had hardly any eggs in it.  I paid one for $15 and it was okay but not good enough to get another one.  The live fish and lobsters, after purchasing them, you have to take them to a different tent to cook for you and there was a long line.  I had to wait for 30 minutes for jambalaya shrimp which had four little shrimp and the rest was rice.   And it was too salty. Seafood paella looked good but again there was a long line.  Overall, I was very disappointed.  There was nothing special about this festival.  I can have live lobsters or crab at home anytime for much less price.  
."}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "6521 Pardall Rd", "attributes": {"Ambience": null, "BusinessParking": null, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": null}, "business_stars": 3.5, "categories": "American (Traditional), Restaurants", "city": "Isla Vista", "hours": null, "name": "On the Side", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2010-08-04 21:32:49", "review_stars": 2.0, "review_text": "Meh.

Granted, as a vegetarian I may not be the intended diner of OTS. That being said, I've been a couple times with different omnivorous friends who have ranging impressions of the place. While some of my friends seem to like it, many seemed underwhelmed by the wings, their staple item. I've gotten the artichoke hearts a couple times, which are decent, but offensively overpriced. This seems to be the moral of On the Side's story.

Possibly the place's saving grace is their great selection of brews. Unfortunately, their selection comes with a price. They have a bunch of flat screens, so I'd say this is a good place to grab a drink and watch a game, but I wouldn't recommend it much further than that."}, {"review_date": "2010-07-15 17:47:10", "review_stars": 3.0, "review_text": "They changed the way you order which is TOTAL CRAP!!! Instead of resteraunt style ordering everyone has to order up at the counter now which is just ridiculous. They need to change this back again ASAP!"}, {"review_date": "2010-06-24 00:21:25", "review_stars": 4.0, "review_text": "Good food. The portions looked kinda small at first, but was full by the time I finished everything. My favorite item is the buffalo wings, they might be some of the best in santa barbara. The service was like whatevers, the waitress was kind of a noob and forgot about taking back the bill so i had to go up to the counter and pay there."}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "7020 Market Place Dr", "attributes": {"Ambience": null, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": true, "street": false, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": null}, "business_stars": 2.5, "categories": "Restaurants, Japanese", "city": "Goleta", "hours": null, "name": "Mika", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2011-08-31 03:46:28", "review_stars": 2.0, "review_text": "Had the Ai Roll Ai Roll, not very good... I mean it's edible and tastes okay.. but I don't think it justifies the price."}, {"review_date": "2011-08-25 19:38:36", "review_stars": 1.0, "review_text": "Chicken bowl was disappointing. When I asked for white meat only they informed me that they only carry dark meat.... 

I consider myself to be pretty easy to please,considering my college budget, however I'm pretty sure I will never eat there again...unless forced.


I will not be returning, no matter what they change the name too."}, {"review_date": "2011-08-11 15:30:57", "review_stars": 1.0, "review_text": "So I came with a group of co-workers after tring to figure out a place to eat. I was craving something somewhat healthy so I went with the Teriyaki chicken bowl. I asked for brown rice but they only serve white. the chicken tasted rubbery and they loaded they soaked the bowl with sauce. Even though it was only $6 bucks I wouldn't have spent a $1 on this! The service was extra slow and the staff wasn't friendly. I will not be back."}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "221 Stearns Wharf", "attributes": {"Ambience": {"casual": false, "classy": false, "divey": false, "hipster": false, "intimate": false, "romantic": false, "touristy": true, "trendy": false, "upscale": false}, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": false, "street": false, "valet": false, "validated": true}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": false, "RestaurantsReservations": true, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": "no"}, "business_stars": 3.0, "categories": "Restaurants, Fish & Chips, Food, Seafood, American (Traditional), Fast Food, Coffee & Tea, Breakfast & Brunch", "city": "Santa Barbara", "hours": {"Friday": "7:0-17:0", "Monday": "7:0-17:0", "Saturday": "7:0-19:0", "Sunday": "7:0-19:0", "Thursday": "7:0-17:0", "Tuesday": "7:0-17:0", "Wednesday": "7:0-17:0"}, "name": "Char West", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2021-12-26 04:52:35", "review_stars": 1.0, "review_text": "It was the worst fish n chips I've ever had. I believe the fish was tilapia as it tasted muddy. We felt disgusted after eating there. The same type of fish was used in the fish taco. We were hungry and was super disappointed with the meal. If you want to eat muddy tasty fish, you can give it a try. It's worst than the frozen fish from the grocery store."}, {"review_date": "2021-11-09 18:16:50", "review_stars": 4.0, "review_text": "Nice stop on the pier for coffee

This is a no frills, no fuss, coffee shop (but also serves  food?!) right on the edge of the pier.  It looks like they are not getting extremely high marks for food, but if you go into the place it doesn't feel like a spot for a gourmet meal. What it is great for, and why I'm giving it four stars, is because of the beautiful view over the pier.  It has some awesome seating on the rail, right outside. I suggest going there early in the morning, maybe even for sunrise, and getting a coffee. I also grabbed a bagel, toasted with cream cheese. It felt like a Bagel experience you would have at Starbucks or coffee bean. 

Stop in for the coffee and the views!"}, {"review_date": "2021-10-17 17:55:00", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Absolutely my favorite spot for breakfast in Santa Barbara! Casual outdoor dining area on Stearns wharf with absolutely gorgeous view of the ocean and the hills of Santa Barbara. Francisco, Blanca and the rest of the staff are always friendly and offer excellent service. They serve a range of espresso drinks, and a nice breakfast (and lunch) menu. My personal favorite is the huevos rancheros.  A great place to eat and appreciate the beauty of Santa Barbara."}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "1201 State St", "attributes": {"Ambience": null, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": false, "street": true, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": null}, "business_stars": 3.0, "categories": "Bars, Restaurants, Nightlife, Barbeque", "city": "Santa Barbara", "hours": null, "name": "State & A Bar and Grill", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2012-07-17 01:38:31", "review_stars": 2.0, "review_text": "Flashback!  My old happy hour spot. Great outdoor patio. Glad I got one last visit in. They are closed now and new restaurant is on the way."}, {"review_date": "2012-06-14 14:12:39", "review_stars": 2.0, "review_text": "food was good, maybe a little over priced, but what they lacked in quality they made up for in customer service."}, {"review_date": "2011-04-13 11:15:00", "review_stars": 1.0, "review_text": "I seriously thought I was on candid camera or something.  I came in for a late lunch one day and everything I got here was absolutely wretched...even their drinks!

Its such a shame because they have a great location and a nice outdoor patio...how do they stay in business??

I must say this place also gets an award: the absolute worst calamari I've ever sampled in my life (and that's saying something)."}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "5701 Calle Real", "attributes": {"Ambience": {"casual": true, "classy": false, "divey": false, "hipster": null, "intimate": false, "romantic": false, "touristy": false, "trendy": true, "upscale": false}, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": true, "street": false, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": "free"}, "business_stars": 4.5, "categories": "Restaurants, Japanese, Ramen", "city": "Goleta", "hours": {"Friday": "17:0-21:30", "Saturday": "17:0-21:30", "Sunday": "17:0-21:30", "Thursday": "17:0-21:30", "Tuesday": "17:0-21:30", "Wednesday": "17:0-21:30"}, "name": "Nikka Ramen", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2022-01-19 06:15:16", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Amazing place, great food , great location. The atmosphere was fun, the music was great. I can tell it's a very popular spot. Servers are very attentive. I will definitely go back again."}, {"review_date": "2022-01-18 01:53:38", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Officially my favorite ramen spot. We don't live in the area but now make it a point to stop by and satisfy our Nikka craving whenever we're in Goleta.

The gyoza was a yummy appetizer but the spicy tuna was sooooo goood! I could eat 10 of those! The basic pork tonkatsu was just as delicious as I remember. Al dente noodles and broth cooked to perfection. The pork chashu is A1 quality. Every ingredient was meant to be on that plate from the tender pork chunks to the salad to the soft boiled egg.

We love Nikka. Period."}, {"review_date": "2022-01-07 01:34:51", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Holly F@ck... mind blowing. Literally spent the last 20 minutes of my life having a mouth gasm. My knees are weak, And ima little sweaty. This ramen just had its way with me.... and I liked it"}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "633 E Cabrillo Blvd", "attributes": {"Ambience": {"casual": false, "classy": false, "divey": false, "hipster": false, "intimate": false, "romantic": false, "touristy": false, "trendy": false, "upscale": false}, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": true, "street": false, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": false, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "RestaurantsReservations": true, "RestaurantsTakeOut": false, "WiFi": "paid"}, "business_stars": 3.5, "categories": "Bars, Hotels, Restaurants, Steakhouses, Hotels & Travel, Seafood, Nightlife, Event Planning & Services, Wine Bars", "city": "Santa Barbara", "hours": {"Friday": "17:0-22:0", "Saturday": "17:0-22:0", "Thursday": "17:0-22:0", "Tuesday": "17:0-22:0", "Wednesday": "17:0-22:0"}, "name": "Rodney's Grill", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2018-11-24 18:54:58", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Amazing dinner at Rodney's Grill.  The foie gras was the best I've ever eaten! And the steak with chantrells was heavenly!  Kudos to this new chef, Chef Moissin!!!  Thanks for making our Thanksgiving dinner so awesome!  Our waitress from Montenegro was super nice also!"}, {"review_date": "2018-11-23 02:15:24", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "I know the chef is new and that the Hilton just took over this location, but we had our Thanksgiving dinner there today, and it felt like they had always been there. From the greeting at the door, to the service, the cocktails, the meals, it was excellent. Can't wait to go back for dinner on a non holiday. FYI the picky eater ate every single bit of his Turkey dinner... the lobster risotto was flawless with the fish course."}, {"review_date": "2017-11-11 03:48:11", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "I got the Pecan crusted halibut and it was amazingly scrumptious delicious awesomeness.   Whatever the buttery sauce was that comes with it literally made fireworks go off inside of me when I ate it.  

My wife had the Kansas City strip steak and it also was really good.  Her sauce was a red wine reduction and it was also incredible.  

We had the Parker station Pino Noir red wine and it was smooth and delicious."}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "413 State St", "attributes": {"Ambience": {"casual": null, "classy": false, "divey": null, "hipster": null, "intimate": null, "romantic": null, "touristy": false, "trendy": null, "upscale": null}, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": true, "street": false, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": null, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": "free"}, "business_stars": 4.5, "categories": "Diners, Restaurants, Breakfast & Brunch", "city": "Santa Barbara", "hours": {"Friday": "7:30-13:30", "Monday": "0:0-0:0", "Saturday": "7:30-14:0", "Sunday": "8:0-14:0", "Thursday": "7:30-13:30", "Tuesday": "7:30-13:30", "Wednesday": "7:30-13:30"}, "name": "JJ’s Diner", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2021-12-30 20:27:18", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "My husband and I were looking for a breakfast place while staying in Santa Barbara. We walked by this place and decided to try it out. First we were greeted with kind smiles and did not have to wait to be seated. Michael was our server and he was so so so kind! We ordered the Chile Verde Omelette and Eggs with Bacon. We received our food fast! The food was great, the service was amazing, and the environment was great!

Give this place a try!"}, {"review_date": "2021-12-29 01:04:47", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Great breakfast and service. Highly recommend. Staff even took care of noisy transients as they came on by - thank goodness !"}, {"review_date": "2021-12-28 19:02:22", "review_stars": 4.0, "review_text": "The wait to be seated was short despite the long line, they work quickly to get your food in front of you. The Customer service at this place is awesome and deserves 5 stars by itself. They are very friendly, prompt, and kept our coffees filled. If you notice the other reviews where Karens were complaining about bad service, were leaving reviews around when covid peaked so don't pay attention to those. I assure you the service is great.

The food is not bad, however it is basic, and safe. Don't get me wrong,  the food tasted fine, it's just that they play it safe which I guess is a good thing so that Karens in SB (There are plenty in this town) don't complain."}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "700 State St", "attributes": {"Ambience": null, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": false, "street": true, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": null}, "business_stars": 3.0, "categories": "Tex-Mex, Restaurants", "city": "Santa Barbara", "hours": null, "name": "Left At Albuquerque", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2010-01-13 20:29:31", "review_stars": 4.0, "review_text": "Was here visiting from out of town. Stayed for most of happy hour a couple days. killer margaritas. And huge selection of tequilas too. 

The reason I gave it a great review is they had an appetizer I have never been able to find anywhere else. It was called "Ball of Fire" "For people that like really hot or just plain lunatics" It was a Habanero Popper. Like a jalapeno popper but WAYYYYY hotter. It was fun trying to cool off with more beer or margaritas. Thank God we had a ride back home. Anyhow great memory & we really enjoyed the chips and salsa & the happy hours."}, {"review_date": "2009-10-05 21:23:14", "review_stars": 1.0, "review_text": "It was all wrong from the moment I asked if we could sit at the bar to have an appetizer and drinks, and the girl that was seating us said, "yes," but we must order an appetizer.  Then she proceeded to take us out to the patio which confused me because I asked for the bar, but I dismissed that.  She sat us at a table, and we ordered our appetizer and drinks from the server.  He comes back with our drinks and explains that they may ask us to move inside because the patio is reserved for customers ordering dinners rather than just appetizers and drinks.  The patio was not full at all, and we told him we were told that we could order an appetizer alone, but still he said we may have to move later as that is the rule.  No apologies at all.  Ugh - I wanted to leave right after his comment...but I figured I should have my beer first.   First, we never asked to be seated outside; second, if that is a rule at the restaurant, why did they seat us outside when we specifically asked for the bar and told the seater that we were only ordering appetizer and drinks?  

Oh, the appetizer was not so great, but we didn't order anything fancy.  It's possible their other food is really good though.  The server spilled my beer on my sunglasses :( .  We quickly had our drinks and appetizer, paid, then got out of there."}, {"review_date": "2009-09-23 21:14:27", "review_stars": 3.0, "review_text": "Great outdoor patio area.  Loved the ambiance.  The chips and salsa are good, food was okay.  Nothing special."}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "4502 Carpinteria Ave", "attributes": {"Ambience": null, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": false, "street": true, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": null, "RestaurantsReservations": null, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": null}, "business_stars": 4.0, "categories": "Mexican, Restaurants, Grocery, Food", "city": "Carpinteria", "hours": {"Friday": "7:0-23:0", "Monday": "7:0-23:0", "Saturday": "7:0-23:0", "Sunday": "7:0-23:0", "Thursday": "7:0-23:0", "Tuesday": "7:0-23:0", "Wednesday": "7:0-23:0"}, "name": "Fiesta Market & Deli", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2022-01-17 20:13:50", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Best burritos in town! Excellent customer service. If they don't carry it they will to try to order it for you."}, {"review_date": "2021-11-17 22:10:44", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "We stopped here with our fifth-wheel trailer. We parked a few blocks up the street.

The food was freshly made and delicious. We tried the Machaca burrito and the chicken fajitas. Best Mexican ever in Carpenteria! 

The market also stocks a huge selection of beer and wine. The cherry on top was finding our favorite Mexican beer that is difficult to find in LA."}, {"review_date": "2021-07-25 03:55:43", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "Woww my friend recommended lunch from this place and honestly it just might be my new favorite spot in town! We shared nachos and a torta and the torta was literally the same size as a Costco chicken bake. I was literally expecting it to be half of that size. My order came out to $21 and this could have easily fed 3 people, so you definitely get your moneys worth! Wait time might take about 15-20 minutes since they are always super busy!"}], "state": "CA"}

{"address": "1187 Coast Village Rd", "attributes": {"Ambience": {"casual": false, "classy": false, "divey": false, "hipster": false, "intimate": false, "romantic": false, "touristy": false, "trendy": false, "upscale": false}, "BusinessParking": {"garage": false, "lot": false, "street": true, "valet": false, "validated": false}, "Music": null, "OutdoorSeating": true, "RestaurantsGoodForGroups": true, "RestaurantsReservations": false, "RestaurantsTakeOut": true, "WiFi": "no"}, "business_stars": 3.0, "categories": "Pizza, Restaurants", "city": "Santa Barbara", "hours": null, "name": "Giovanni's", "review_info": [{"review_date": "2019-01-08 15:17:24", "review_stars": 4.0, "review_text": "Delicious! I go once a week for the lunch special, slice (which is large) and a salad. Service is quick"}, {"review_date": "2018-12-02 22:16:29", "review_stars": 5.0, "review_text": "The pizza here is so yummy!
